# libFuzzer's own outputs, and the distinction between the two directories beside this file is the
# point of it:
#
#   * `seeds/<target>/` is TRACKED. Hand-written inputs, plus any crash a fuzzer found and somebody
#     read - an entry there arrives through a pull request, and `just fuzz-smoke` replays exactly it.
#   * `corpus/<target>/` is libFuzzer's WORKING corpus. It grows by thousands of files during a
#     run, so committing it would put machine-generated bytes nobody read into the tree - and,
#     measured, it also broke `just hygiene`: a local run left CRLF-carrying generated units in the
#     tree and `line-endings` failed on ten of them.
corpus/
target/
artifacts/
coverage/
